**Plan the 40 minutes.** Confirm the requirements, then build in layers so you always have something working: (1) render N boxes and type in them; (2) auto-advance focus; (3) backspace and arrow keys; (4) paste; (5) validation and submit; (6) polish. Say aloud which layer you are on.

**Structure.**

```html
<div id="otp"></div>
```

```js
const LEN = 6;
const root = document.getElementById("otp");
const inputs = [];
for (let i = 0; i < LEN; i++) {
  const el = document.createElement("input");
  el.maxLength = 1; el.inputMode = "numeric"; el.autocomplete = "one-time-code";
  root.appendChild(el); inputs.push(el);
}
```

Use **one delegated listener** on `root` rather than many handlers, and find the index with `inputs.indexOf(e.target)`.

**Behaviours.**
- `input` event: keep only a digit (`value.replace(/\D/g, "")`), then focus the next box if filled.
- `keydown`: on `Backspace` with an empty box, move to the previous box and clear it; `ArrowLeft` and `ArrowRight` move focus.
- `paste`: read `e.clipboardData.getData("text")`, strip non-digits, distribute characters across boxes starting from the current one, focus the last filled, and `preventDefault()`.
- Completion: when all boxes are filled, join values and call a callback or enable Submit.
- Initial focus on the first box, and select content on focus so retyping replaces it.

**Common bugs to avoid:** attaching listeners before elements exist, using `keyup` which causes double handling, not clearing on backspace, off-by-one on the last box, and relying on `keyCode` instead of `e.key`.

**HTML/CSS concepts to revise:** semantic elements and accessibility (labels, `aria-label` for each digit, focus styles), box model, flexbox and grid, specificity and the cascade, `position` values, `em` vs `rem`, and responsive design with media queries.

**If time runs short,** say what you would add (accessibility, error state, resend timer) and be explicit about trade-offs.
